IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cards-domain`
IMPORT `earn-kernel`
IMPORT fixtures

§ `Terms and Conditions for the UOB Lady's Cards`

-- ===========================================================================
-- DOCUMENT. uob-ladys-cards-tnc: "Terms and Conditions for the UOB Lady's
-- Cards", "Updated in August 2025 (Version 1.1)" (United Overseas Bank
-- Limited), cl.1-43 and Schedule 1. It governs the Lady's Classic, Platinum,
-- World Mastercard, Solitaire and Solitaire Metal cards. The guidance FAQ
-- (uob-ladys-faq) repeats the caps and the categories' MCC lists. The savings
-- uplift is a separate document (uob-ladys-savings.l4).
--
-- WHAT THE TEXT SAYS.
--   cl.2(b)-(c) Base UNI$ = UNI$1 per S$5 (0.4 miles per S$1). Bonus UNI$ = 9X
--               UNI$ per S$5 (3.6 miles per S$1) in addition. "Quarter" =
--               Jan-Mar, Apr-Jun, Jul-Sep, Oct-Dec.
--   cl.3        "UNI$ can be converted to KrisFlyer or Asia miles (in blocks of
--               10,000 miles) at the conversion rate of UNI$1 = 2 miles."
--   cl.4-5      Classic, Platinum and World Mastercard choose ONE Preferred
--               Rewards Category; Solitaire and Solitaire Metal choose TWO. The
--               first selection applies that Quarter; later ones from the next
--               Quarter; "If you do not select or change ... the current
--               selected category(s) shall continue".
--   cl.6        The Bonus UNI$ per calendar month is capped: Classic, Platinum,
--               World Mastercard 1,800 UNI$ (S$1,000); Solitaire, with effect from 1
--               August 2025, 2,700 UNI$ (S$1,500) with each Preferred Rewards
--               Category capped at 1,350 UNI$ (S$750); Solitaire Metal 3,600 UNI$
--               (S$2,000).
--   cl.8        "any Base UNI$ and Bonus UNI$ ... will be computed based on the
--               date that the transaction is posted on UOB's systems."
--   cl.10       Foreign-currency transactions are converted to Singapore dollars
--               and "the Singapore dollar amount of all transactions ... posted"
--               is used.
--   cl.17       No UNI$ for a purchase converted into the Lady's LuxePay Plan.
--   cl.32, 34, 35, 33  What earns nothing: kinds, MCCs, descriptions.
--   Schedule 1  The seven categories and the MCCs they are "automatically
--               categorised" by: Beauty & Wellness 5912, 5977, 7230, 7231, 7298,
--               7297; Dining 5811, 5812, 5814, 5499; Entertainment 5813, 7832,
--               7922; Family 5411, 5641; Fashion 5311, 5611, 5621, 5631, 5651,
--               5655, 5661, 5691, 5699, 5948; Transport 4111, 4121, 4789, 5541,
--               5542; Travel: "Credit card retail transaction(s) made at major
--               airlines and/or hotels with their main business activity
--               classified as flights and/or hotels only. (including card-not-
--               present transactions like ecommerce/mail/phone order
--               transactions)". The MCC "determines whether the transaction is
--               eligible for Bonus UNI$ under each category ... we cannot
--               guarantee that a transaction will fall within your selected
--               Preferred Rewards Category(ies)."
--
-- THE FORKS.
--   F-uob-per-five: floor on whole S$5 blocks, ceiling pro rata.
--   F-ladys-travel: Travel is defined by the merchant's main business, not by an
--     MCC. The module uses airline and lodging MCCs (3000-3350, 4511; 3501-3999,
--     7011) as the stand-in and names the open reading for a Travel answer.
--   F-ladys-metal-categories: Solitaire Metal's cap is stated as one total
--     (3,600 UNI$), with no per-category cap; the module shares it across the
--     two categories.
--   F-bill-payments: cl.32(a) "Bill payment (where applicable)": a bill paid
--     directly on the card is the open reading; floor 0, ceiling the full earn.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `cl.32, cl.34, cl.35, cl.17, cl.33 -- what earns nothing`

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the Lady's excluded category codes` MEANS
    LIST 4829, 4900, 5199, 5960, 5965, 5993, 6012, 6050, 6051, 6211, 6300, 6513, 6529, 6530, 6534,
         6540, 7349, 7511, 7523, 7995, 8062, 8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299, 8398, 8651, 8661,
         8699, 8999, 9211, 9222, 9223, 9311, 9399, 9402, 9405

GIVEN k IS A `Charge kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Lady's cl.32 excludes the kind` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `Retail purchase`                                   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Bill payment`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Top-up of a prepaid card or stored-value account`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Payment of funds to a payment service provider`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Instalment plan charge`                            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `My Preferred Payment Plan charge`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Cash advance`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Balance transfer or funds transfer`                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Fee, interest or finance charge`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Pre-authorisation`                                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Payment through UOB Payment Facility`              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `NETS or NETS-related transaction`                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SmartPay or personal loan`                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Transit-related transaction`                       THEN FALSE

-- cl.35: the listed descriptions, each "*" meaning any characters may follow.
-- This list, unlike the PRVI, Preferred Visa and Visa Signature lists, names
-- PAYPAL* without qualification, City Index, PLUS500 and YOUTRIP.
GIVEN d IS A Descriptor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Lady's cl.35 lists the description` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `AXS`                                                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Amaze`                                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Amaze with a transit or payment counterparty`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `EZ-Link`                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `FlashPay`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `NETS VCashCard`                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `TRANSIT`                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Transit Link`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Youtrip`                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Razerpay`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SingPost-SAM`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `iPayMy`                                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SmoovPay`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `PayPal`                                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `PayPal Bizconsulta or Capitalroya or Oandaasiapa`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Moneybookers`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Skrill`                                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `OANDA`                                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Saxo`                                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `IG Markets`                                           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Plus500`                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `City Index`                                           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SkyFX`                                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Banc de Binary`                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `RWS-Levy`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `NORWDS`                                               THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                                        FALSE

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Lady's card excludes the purchase` p MEANS
    `Lady's cl.32 excludes the kind` (p's `charge kind`)
    OR `the code is among` p `the Lady's excluded category codes`
    OR `Lady's cl.35 lists the description` (p's descriptor)
    OR p's `later reversed`


§§ `Schedule 1 -- the categories`

GIVEN cat IS A `Solitaire category`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the Lady's Schedule 1 codes for` cat MEANS
    CONSIDER cat
    WHEN `Beauty & Wellness` THEN LIST 5912, 5977, 7230, 7231, 7298, 7297
    WHEN `Dining`            THEN LIST 5811, 5812, 5814, 5499
    WHEN `Entertainment`     THEN LIST 5813, 7832, 7922
    WHEN `Family`            THEN LIST 5411, 5641
    WHEN `Fashion`           THEN LIST 5311, 5611, 5621, 5631, 5651, 5655, 5661, 5691, 5699, 5948
    WHEN `Transport`         THEN LIST 4111, 4121, 4789, 5541, 5542
    WHEN `Travel`            THEN EMPTY

-- The Travel stand-in (fork F-ladys-travel): an airline MCC or a lodging MCC.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the code of the purchase is an airline or hotel code` p MEANS
    `the code is from` p 3000 3350
    OR `the code is among` p (LIST 4511, 7011)
    OR `the code is from` p 3501 3999

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
      cat IS A `Solitaire category`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Lady's purchase falls in` p `the category` cat MEANS
    IF cat EQUALS `Travel`
    THEN `the code of the purchase is an airline or hotel code` p
    ELSE `the code is among` p (`the Lady's Schedule 1 codes for` cat)

-- The first of her elected categories that the purchase falls in, if any.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
      cats IS A LIST OF `Solitaire category`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Solitaire category`
`the elected Lady's category that the purchase falls in among` p cats MEANS
    CONSIDER cats
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `the Lady's purchase falls in` p `the category` first
        THEN JUST first
        ELSE `the elected Lady's category that the purchase falls in among` p rest


§§ `cl.6 -- the caps`

GIVEN c IS A Card
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Lady's card elects two categories` c MEANS
    c EQUALS `UOB Lady's Solitaire` OR c EQUALS `UOB Lady's Solitaire Metal`

-- The Bonus UNI$ cap that a category is held to, by card (cl.6(a)-(c)). The
-- Solitaire Metal figure is one total for both categories (fork
-- F-ladys-metal-categories).
GIVEN c IS A Card
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Lady's Bonus UNI$ cap per calendar month for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `UOB Lady's Classic`            THEN 1800
    WHEN `UOB Lady's Platinum`           THEN 1800
    WHEN `UOB Lady's World Mastercard`   THEN 1800
    WHEN `UOB Lady's Solitaire`          THEN 1350
    WHEN `UOB Lady's Solitaire Metal`    THEN 3600
    OTHERWISE                                 0

-- The position of a category among her elected ones.
GIVEN cat IS A `Solitaire category`
      cats IS A LIST OF `Solitaire category`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the position of` cat `among her elected categories` cats MEANS
    CONSIDER cats
    WHEN EMPTY THEN -1
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF cat EQUALS first
        THEN 0
        ELSE IF (`the position of` cat `among her elected categories` rest) AT LEAST 0
             THEN 1 PLUS (`the position of` cat `among her elected categories` rest)
             ELSE -1

-- The Bonus UNI$ she has earned so far in the category, from the month record.
GIVEN cat IS A `Solitaire category`
      h IS A `Lady's holder`
      m IS A `Lady's month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Bonus UNI$ earned so far in` cat `by the holder` h `in the month` m MEANS
    IF (`the position of` cat `among her elected categories` (h's `elected categories`)) AT LEAST 0
    THEN at (m's `Bonus UNI$ by elected category`) (`the position of` cat `among her elected categories` (h's `elected categories`))
    ELSE 0

-- Room left under the cap for a purchase in this category, in UNI$.
GIVEN cat IS A `Solitaire category`
      c IS A Card
      h IS A `Lady's holder`
      m IS A `Lady's month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Lady's Bonus UNI$ room in` cat `on` c `for the holder` h `in the month` m MEANS
    IF c EQUALS `UOB Lady's Solitaire Metal`
    THEN `at least nothing` ((`the Lady's Bonus UNI$ cap per calendar month for` c) MINUS (sum (m's `Bonus UNI$ by elected category`)))
    ELSE `at least nothing` ((`the Lady's Bonus UNI$ cap per calendar month for` c) MINUS (`the Bonus UNI$ earned so far in` cat `by the holder` h `in the month` m))


§§ `The arithmetic: a basic UNI$1 and a bonus UNI$9 per S$5, the bonus capped`

-- UNI$1 = 2 miles (cl.3).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`miles per UNI$ for the Lady's cards` MEANS 2

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Lady's whole S$5 blocks in` amount MEANS
    FLOOR (amount DIVIDED BY 5)

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      room IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Lady's total UNI$ by blocks` amount room MEANS
    (`Lady's whole S$5 blocks in` amount) PLUS (min ((`Lady's whole S$5 blocks in` amount) TIMES 9) room)

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      room IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Lady's total UNI$ pro rata` amount room MEANS
    FLOOR ((amount DIVIDED BY 5) PLUS (min ((amount TIMES 9) DIVIDED BY 5) room))

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Lady's base UNI$` amount MEANS
    FLOOR (amount DIVIDED BY 5)

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      room IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF Condition
`Lady's rounding conditions at` amount room MEANS
    IF `Lady's total UNI$ by blocks` amount room EQUALS `Lady's total UNI$ pro rata` amount room
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`


§§ `The answer when the code is settled`

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      room IS A NUMBER
      thePot IS A Pot
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Lady's answer at the bonus rate` c p room thePot MEANS
    `an answer for` c `in` `UNI$` `of` (`Lady's total UNI$ by blocks` (p's `amount in SGD`) room) `to` (`Lady's total UNI$ pro rata` (p's `amount in SGD`) room) `wanting` ((`Lady's whole S$5 blocks in` (p's `amount in SGD`)) TIMES 9) `at` (JUST `miles per UNI$ for the Lady's cards`) `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` thePot `depending on` (`Lady's rounding conditions at` (p's `amount in SGD`) room) `per` "UOB Lady's Cards T&C cl.2(b)-(c), cl.6, Schedule 1"

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Lady's answer at the base rate` c p MEANS
    `an answer for` c `in` `UNI$` `of` (`Lady's base UNI$` (p's `amount in SGD`)) `to` (`Lady's base UNI$` (p's `amount in SGD`)) `wanting` 0 `at` (JUST `miles per UNI$ for the Lady's cards`) `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` `No pot` `depending on` EMPTY `per` "UOB Lady's Cards T&C cl.2(b)"

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      h IS A `Lady's holder`
      m IS A `Lady's month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Lady's answer when the code is settled` c p h m MEANS
    IF `the Lady's card excludes the purchase` p
    THEN `nothing is earned on` c `in` `UNI$` `per` "UOB Lady's Cards T&C cl.32-35"
    ELSE `Lady's answer in the elected category` c p h m (`the elected Lady's category that the purchase falls in among` p (h's `elected categories`))

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      h IS A `Lady's holder`
      m IS A `Lady's month`
      found IS A MAYBE `Solitaire category`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Lady's answer in the elected category` c p h m found MEANS
    CONSIDER found
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Lady's answer at the base rate` c p
    WHEN JUST cat THEN
        IF cat EQUALS `Travel`
        THEN `bracketed from` (`Lady's answer at the base rate` c p) `to` (`Lady's answer at the bonus rate` c p (`the Lady's Bonus UNI$ room in` cat `on` c `for the holder` h `in the month` m) (`Lady's category` cat)) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)
        ELSE `Lady's answer at the bonus rate` c p (`the Lady's Bonus UNI$ room in` cat `on` c `for the holder` h `in the month` m) (`Lady's category` cat)

GIVEN c IS A Card
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Lady's earns nothing under the open reading` c MEANS
    `nothing is earned on` c `in` `UNI$` `per` "UOB Lady's Cards T&C cl.32(a) (open reading)"

-- A code in the first elected category, for the best case when the code is unknown.
GIVEN cats IS A LIST OF `Solitaire category`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`a code in the first elected category of` cats MEANS
    CONSIDER cats
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 5812
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF first EQUALS `Travel` THEN 3000 ELSE at (`the Lady's Schedule 1 codes for` first) 0

`a Lady's code that is excluded` MEANS 4829

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      h IS A `Lady's holder`
      m IS A `Lady's month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`UOB Lady's card earns on` c p h m MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the code is unknown for` p
            THEN `bracketed from` (`Lady's answer when the code is settled` c (`recoded purchase` p `a Lady's code that is excluded`) h m) `to` (`Lady's answer when the code is settled` c (`recoded purchase` p (`a code in the first elected category of` (h's `elected categories`))) h m) `adding` (LIST `The merchant category code is not known`)
        IF p's `charge kind` EQUALS `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`
            THEN `bracketed from` (`Lady's earns nothing under the open reading` c) `to` (`Lady's answer when the code is settled` c p h m) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)
        OTHERWISE `Lady's answer when the code is settled` c p h m


§§ `cl.5 -- when a selection takes effect`

-- "You may change your selection each Quarter. The first selection made upon
-- registering will be applicable for that Quarter. Subsequent selections will
-- only be applicable to the following Quarter." The first calendar day of the
-- Quarter after the one a date falls in.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the Quarter after` day MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF DATE_MONTH day AT MOST 3 THEN Date 1 4 (DATE_YEAR day)
        IF DATE_MONTH day AT MOST 6 THEN Date 1 7 (DATE_YEAR day)
        IF DATE_MONTH day AT MOST 9 THEN Date 1 10 (DATE_YEAR day)
        OTHERWISE Date 1 1 ((DATE_YEAR day) PLUS 1)


§§ `The clock the Lady's category pot runs on`

-- cl.6 and cl.8.
GIVETH A `Period basis`
`the Lady's category pot's period` MEANS `Calendar month`

GIVETH A `Date basis`
`the Lady's category pot's date basis` MEANS `Posting date`

#ASSERT `the Lady's category pot's period` EQUALS `Calendar month`
#ASSERT `the Lady's category pot's date basis` EQUALS `Posting date`


§§ `Illustrations`

`a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` MEANS `Lady's holder` WITH
    `elected categories`  IS LIST `Dining`, `Family`
    `Lady's Savings band` IS `Under S$10,000`

`a Lady's Classic holder who elected Fashion` MEANS `Lady's holder` WITH
    `elected categories`  IS LIST `Fashion`
    `Lady's Savings band` IS `Under S$10,000`

`a Lady's Solitaire Metal holder who elected Dining and Transport` MEANS `Lady's holder` WITH
    `elected categories`  IS LIST `Dining`, `Transport`
    `Lady's Savings band` IS `Under S$10,000`

GIVEN first IS A NUMBER
      second IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Lady's month`
`a Lady's month with` first `and` second `Bonus UNI$ so far` MEANS
    `Lady's month` WITH `Bonus UNI$ by elected category` IS LIST first, second

`a fresh Lady's month` MEANS `a Lady's month with` 0 `and` 0 `Bonus UNI$ so far`

`Solitaire` MEANS `UOB Lady's Solitaire`
`Classic` MEANS `UOB Lady's Classic`
`Metal` MEANS `UOB Lady's Solitaire Metal`

-- Dining: S$100 at a restaurant (5812): UNI$10 per S$5 -> 20 blocks -> 200 UNI$ = 400 miles = 4 mpd.
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` `the base purchase` `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` `the base purchase` `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `miles certain`) EQUALS 400
-- ... fast food and food delivery are Dining (5814), as are 5811 caterers and 5499.
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5814) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5499) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5811) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
-- ... a bakery (5462), a bar (5813) and a toy shop (5945) are not Dining or Family: base only, UNI$20.
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5462) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5813) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5945) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
-- ... Family: supermarkets (5411) and children's wear (5641).
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5411) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5641) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
-- ... a marketplace (5262) and EV charging (5552) earn the base.
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5262) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5552) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20

-- cl.6(b): each category capped at 1,350 Bonus UNI$ (S$750). With 1,350 in Dining, S$100 at a restaurant earns the base only.
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` `the base purchase` `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` (`a Lady's month with` 1350 `and` 0 `Bonus UNI$ so far`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
-- ... the Family pot is separate: S$100 at a supermarket still earns the bonus.
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5411) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` (`a Lady's month with` 1350 `and` 0 `Bonus UNI$ so far`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
-- ... with 1,300 earned, 50 UNI$ of room remain: 20 base + 50 bonus = 70.
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` `the base purchase` `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` (`a Lady's month with` 1300 `and` 0 `Bonus UNI$ so far`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 70
-- ... the bonus wanted before the cap is 20 blocks x 9 = 180.
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` `the base purchase` `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` (`a Lady's month with` 1350 `and` 0 `Bonus UNI$ so far`))'s `bonus units before cap` EQUALS 180
-- The pot named is the elected category's.
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` `the base purchase` `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s pot EQUALS `Lady's category` `Dining`
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Solitaire` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5411) `a Lady's Solitaire holder who elected Dining and Family` `a fresh Lady's month`)'s pot EQUALS `Lady's category` `Family`

-- cl.6(a): the Classic family holds one category with a 1,800 cap (S$1,000).
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Classic` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5651) `a Lady's Classic holder who elected Fashion` (`Lady's month` WITH `Bonus UNI$ by elected category` IS LIST 0))'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Classic` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5651) `a Lady's Classic holder who elected Fashion` (`Lady's month` WITH `Bonus UNI$ by elected category` IS LIST 1800))'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Classic` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5812) `a Lady's Classic holder who elected Fashion` (`Lady's month` WITH `Bonus UNI$ by elected category` IS LIST 0))'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
-- cl.6(c): the Metal card shares 3,600 across both categories.
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Metal` `the base purchase` `a Lady's Solitaire Metal holder who elected Dining and Transport` (`a Lady's month with` 1800 `and` 1800 `Bonus UNI$ so far`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`UOB Lady's card earns on` `Metal` `the base purchase` `a Lady's Solitaire Metal holder who elected Dining and Transport` (`a Lady's month with` 1800 `and` 1700 `Bonus UNI$ so far`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 120

-- Schedule 1 spot checks: Beauty, Entertainment, Fashion, Transport.
#ASSERT `the Lady's purchase falls in` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5977) `the category` `Beauty & Wellness`
#ASSERT `the Lady's purchase falls in` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 7298) `the category` `Beauty & Wellness`
#ASSERT `the Lady's purchase falls in` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 7922) `the category` `Entertainment`
#ASSERT `the Lady's purchase falls in` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5948) `the category` `Fashion`
